Package: gcanvas
Type: Package
Title: Genomic Visualization and Analysis Toolkit
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(
    given = "Beomsu", family = "Kim",
    email = "bk.statg@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7410-4273"))
Description: A toolkit for visualizing and analyzing genomic association data,
    including Manhattan, Q-Q, regional, Miami, circos, and heterozygosity-
    missingness plots; principal component analysis with reference projection
    and ancestry estimation; LD computation, clumping, and proxy lookup;
    GTF-driven gene/exon tracks; liftover; and assorted helpers for working
    with GWAS summary statistics.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/stat-gene/gcanvas
BugReports: https://github.com/stat-gene/gcanvas/issues
SystemRequirements: Some functions shell out to external command-line tools
    (install only what your workflow needs). PLINK 2
    (https://www.cog-genomics.org/plink/2.0/) for pca(), pca.projection(),
    plink.extract(), hetmiss(); PLINK 1.9
    (https://www.cog-genomics.org/plink/1.9/) is additionally required for the
    multi-input merge step of plink.extract(). UCSC liftOver for liftover()
    (recommended install: conda install bioconda::ucsc-liftover; or download
    from https://hgdownload.soe.ucsc.edu/admin/exe/); chain files for the
    common build pairs are bundled. tabix/htslib
    (http://www.htslib.org/) for the GTF paths of gtf2rds(), regional(), and
    geneinfo().
